-- cmd: repl
-- stdin: type P { A, B }\nlet a1 = A\nlet b1 = B\ntype P { B, A }\na1 < b1\nA < B\n:quit\n
-- Redefinition is early-bound (stage 5 decision D4): after `P` is
-- declared again with its variants in the other order, the values of
-- the old `P` keep the old order, and the new `P`'s values have the new
-- one.
